title: Bump trie-db to 0.33.0 and hash-db to 0.17.0
doc:
- audience: [Node Operator, Runtime Dev]
  description: |
    trie-db 0.33.0 fixes removing a key that is not in the trie but is a strict prefix of a stored
    key (paritytech/trie#249). trie-db 0.32.0 panicked or deleted the stored key's value; now the
    removal does nothing. A bug-free runtime cannot do this (FRAME storage never removes such a
    key), only a removal of raw keys like system.kill_storage by root. Still, it changes the
    storage root of such a block.

    Sync the chain from genesis with the new node before upgrading; all system chains do.

    Also: hash-db HashDB and PlainDB no longer require Send + Sync (paritytech/trie#214), and
    TrieDBMut writes the root only in commit (paritytech/trie#250).
crates:
- name: sp-trie
  bump: major
- name: sp-core
  bump: major
- name: sp-api
  bump: major
- name: sp-state-machine
  bump: major
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: major
- name: sc-client-api
  bump: major
- name: binary-merkle-tree
  bump: major
- name: bp-runtime
  bump: major
- name: sc-client-db
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: minor
- name: substrate-state-trie-migration-rpc
  bump: minor
- name: sp-crypto-hashing
